-- This file rebuilt `events` and `registrations` with UUID primary keys. It is
-- wrong in two ways that were expensive to discover:
--
--   1. It opens with DROP TABLE registrations CASCADE / DROP TABLE events
--      CASCADE. Another teammate's app owns those tables. Running this
--      destroys their data and violates hard constraint #1 (never DROP TABLE).
--
--   2. Its UUID ids contradict the live schema, where events.id,
--      registrations.event_id and registrations.user_id are all varchar(64).
--      This exact uuid-vs-varchar mismatch, left behind in decision_log, is
--      what broke Gate 1 (22P02 "invalid input syntax for type uuid") until
--      006_decision_log_varchar.sql widened the column.
--
-- The correct approach is ADDITIVE and already applied:
--   005_additive.sql              - adds the four columns we need
--   006_decision_log_varchar.sql  - widens decision_log.event_id to varchar(64)
--
-- Every statement below is commented out, so this file is a no-op even if it
-- is executed by accident. Do not uncomment it.
-- ============================================================================

